## RULES

```elixir
if :global.whereis_name(:main) != :undefined, do: Main.stop()
```

```elixir
rules=
"""
cmd cmdZ { sleep 30 && echo "long running command" } only, node0;

cmd cmdA { mkdir -p $HOME/JAR_OF_DIRT } low, node0;

cmd cmdB { cd $HOME/JAR_OF_DIRT && touch amazing && echo bye } node0;

cmd cmdC { echo "hello from node1" } node1;

cmd cmdD { echo "hello from node2" } node2;

run cmdZ;
run cmdA then cmdB;
run cmdC;
run cmdD;
"""

{cmds, rules} = ExMan.loadrules(rules)
:ok
```

```elixir
{:ok, pid} = Main.initialize(cmds, rules)
```

```elixir
Main.run_exp()
```

```elixir
Main.get_state()
```

